{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>which the man would call it, a living soul</b>. The language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 2:19): rearrange it and explicate it as — 'and every living soul that the man would call a name, that is its name forever.' And Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 2:19) said that the לָמֶ\"ד of 'אֲשֶׁר יִקְרָא לוֹ' (which he would call it) carries over, so that it means: 'and all that the man would call a living soul, that is its name forever.' And it is possible that its meaning concerns the matter of a helper, and the intention is to say that the man is a living soul, as it says, 'and the man became a living soul' (Genesis 2:7), as I have explained. And He brought before him all the species, and every species among them that the man would call by its name and say of it that it is a living soul like himself — that would be its name and it would be for him as a helper corresponding to him. But he called to all of them and did not find for himself a helper that he could call 'living soul' like his own name."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:23:48.972984054Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}